AI-Powered Income Prediction Tool - Technical Overview
📌 Project Overview
This project is an AI-based Income Prediction System that estimates whether an individual’s annual income is above or below $50K based on various socio-economic factors. The model was trained as part of my Professional Training 1 (PT-1) in my last semester at Sathyabama Institute of Science and Technology, Chennai.

It utilizes data from the UCI Adult Dataset, which includes demographic and employment-related attributes. The model is trained using a supervised learning algorithm to classify income levels based on these features.

📊 Data Preprocessing & Features
The dataset contains 48,842 records and 14 features, including both numerical and categorical variables:

Numerical Features: Age, Education-Num, Capital-Gain, Capital-Loss, Hours-Per-Week
Categorical Features: Workclass, Education Level, Marital-Status, Occupation, Relationship, Race, Sex, Native-Country
To preprocess the data:

Handled Missing Values: Removed rows containing missing categorical values
Encoding Categorical Variables: Applied one-hot encoding to transform categorical data
Feature Scaling: Normalized numerical features to bring them to a similar scale
Balanced Classes: The dataset had a class imbalance between high-income and low-income groups, which was addressed using class weighting
📌 Technical Details:
✔ Dataset Used: UCI Adult Dataset (Census Income Data)
✔ Feature Engineering: One-hot encoding for categorical features
✔ Machine Learning Model: Random Forest Classifier (100 estimators, Gini Impurity, Max Depth tuning)
✔️ Training & Testing Split: 80-20% split (Stratified Sampling)
✔️ Hyperparameter Tuning: Used Grid Search CV for optimal hyperparameters
✔️ Performance Metrics: Accuracy, Precision, Recall, F1-score, ROC-AUC

📊 Deployment Details:
✔ Frontend: Gradio UI for easy user interaction (Sliders & Dropdowns for input features)
✔ Backend & Model Implementation: Python, scikit-learn, pandas, NumPy
✔ Hosting Platform: Hugging Face Spaces using Gradio Interface
✔ Inference: Takes user inputs, processes categorical variables, applies feature encoding, and runs predictions in real time

